## geolize-studio/laravel-chile

The published `geolize-studio/laravel-chile` release is `0.1.0`, installed from Packagist with `composer require "geolize-studio/laravel-chile:^0.1"`. This source-checkout guideline also describes unreleased `0.2` RUT improvements. Compact input, `RutFormat`, `withFormat()`, and `chile.rut.format` require that development source. Source repository https://github.com/Geolize-Studio/laravel-chile. During `0.x`, APIs may change in minor releases. Review the changelog before widening the version constraint. Inspect installed source, tests, Composer metadata, and released version before using or documenting an API. Do not invent classes, commands, configuration, or exports.

Its `0.1` domain is limited to RUT, the Chilean region → province → comuna hierarchy with CUT codes, and exact whole-peso CLP / IVA arithmetic. Keep domain code offline and deterministic. Do not add taxpayer lookup, SII/DTE, tax-status decisions, PPU, holidays, phones, UF/UTM, geocoding, carrier rates, AI matching, UI, models, database access, or network calls.

- RUT: parsing, checksum validation, canonical storage, and display are distinct. Never silently repair an invalid verification digit or infer identity, existence, or tax status from a mathematically valid RUT.
- Territory: preserve original input and CUT leading zeroes. Make normalizations and encoding repairs visible. Resolve only exact, normalized, or unambiguous configured aliases; return ambiguity or not-found instead of guessing a comuna.
- CLP and IVA: use signed 64-bit integer pesos and rational rates; reject fractions, floats, malformed input, and overflow. Declare rounding, including ties and negatives, and verify `net + IVA = gross` after rounding. The 19% IVA default does not decide whether IVA applies.

Use `Rut::parse()` / `tryParse()`, `Clp::fromPesos()` / `parse()` / `tryParse()`, `Iva::standard()->fromNet()` / `fromGross()` with an explicit `RoundingMode`, and `Territory::loadDefault()` (or `app(Territory::class)`). The namespace is `GeolizeStudio\Chile`. Territory returns `ComunaResolution` with `status`, `match`, `candidates`, `original`, and `transformations`; check `ResolutionStatus::Matched` before assignment. Rules are under `Laravel\Rules` (`RutRule`, `ClpRule`). Put `Rut::class`, `Clp::class`, and `Iva::class` directly in a model's `casts()` map; explicit `Laravel\Casts\RutCast`, `ClpCast`, and `IvaCast` also exist. Store RUT in a string column, CLP in signed `BIGINT`, and IVA in JSON containing exactly integer `numerator` and `denominator` keys. Assign an `Iva` or ratio array, never a float, percentage, or raw JSON string. Null stays distinct from zero. No fuzzy matcher or encoding-repair API exists.

In the development source, RUT parsing accepts properly grouped or ungrouped bodies with an optional ASCII hyphen, always validating the final DV. Publish `config/chile.php` through `php artisan vendor:publish --tag=chile-config`. `chile.rut.format` selects `canonical` (default), `compact`, or `formatted` for cast writes, cast value string/JSON output, and model array/JSON serialization. `Rut::class.':compact'` overrides the setting per attribute. `Rut::parse()` defaults to canonical output independently of Laravel configuration. Use `withFormat(RutFormat::Compact)` for an immutable output preference or `format(RutFormat)` for explicit rendering. Plain `format()` renders dotted presentation. Size string columns for 9 compact, 10 canonical, or 12 formatted characters. Reading historical values preserves raw storage on an unrelated save. Explicit assignment applies the selected format.

Native string-backed `Region`, `Province`, and `Comuna` enums live in the root namespace. Use `Comuna::Nunoa->value` (`'13120'`), `label()` (`'Ñuñoa'`), `region()`, `province()`, and `Comuna::options(region: Region::Metropolitana)`. Regions expose `provinces()` / `comunas()` and provinces expose `region()` / `comunas()`. Use these enums directly in Laravel casts and `Rule::enum()` with string request validation. Persist string CUT values, never case names or integer codes. Parent relationships require explicit application validation when stored separately. PHP may coerce numeric string option keys to integers; enum values remain strings. These enums represent the bundled catalog; `Territory` namespace records remain available for custom snapshots. Read `docs/enums.md` and `docs/eloquent.md` relative to the installed package root for exact contracts.

Use Laravel adapters only where the installed package exports them. Test adapters with the package's supported Laravel/PHP matrix; keep facades, application models, database access, and global state out of the domain layer. All public documentation is English except proper Chilean terms such as RUT, comuna, CLP, IVA, and CUT.
